  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Sidaga calls a sequence beautiful if the sum of elements of this sequence is strictly positive.\n\nKaspers gave Sidaga a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ and asked him to partition it into exactly KKK non-empty **contiguous** subsequences such that each element of AAA belongs to exactly one subsequence and all KKK subsequences are beautiful.\n\nSidaga is getting ready for his wedding - he is busy learning how to dance, so he cannot solve this problem. Can you help him?",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1,0001 \\le T \\le 1,0001≤T≤1,000",
      "1≤K≤N≤5⋅1051 \\le K \\le N \\le 5 \\cdot 10^51≤K≤N≤5⋅105",
      "0≤∣Ai∣≤1090 \\le |A_i| \\le 10^90≤∣Ai​∣≤109 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 5⋅1055 \\cdot 10^55⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing the string `\"YES\"` if it is possible to partition AAA into KKK contiguous subsequences or `\"NO\"` otherwise.\n\nIf it is possible to partition AAA, print a second line containing KKK space-separated integers B1,B2,…,BKB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_KB1​,B2​,…,BK​ denoting the sizes of the subsequences, where 1≤Bi1 \\le B_i1≤Bi​ for each valid iii and B1+B2+…+BK=NB_1 + B_2 + \\ldots + B_K = NB1​+B2​+…+BK​=N. The first B1B_1B1​ elements of AAA belong to the first subsequence, the next B2B_2B2​ elements belong to the second subsequence and so on.\n\nIf there is more than one solution, you may print any one.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n4 2\n2 -1 1 3 \n2 2\n1 -1",
        "output": "YES\n1 3\nNO",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1:\nIn first case, there are more than one options. Another such valid option is {2,2}.\nIn second case, it is not possible."
      }
    ]
  },
